  "full_text": "Well, entertain God and your ass will follow. I wonder where the microphone is on this camera. Oh, well. Anyway, got a new camera. Wow, look at the... Do you see the glint off the cars? So this is like the solstice, huh? Almost. Not quite. To join with you again. Sound of silence. Fuck you, car. I think one of them died, didn't he? The new camera's a little bit different. Five cheers for mom. She looks well to the ways of her household. Her children rise up and bless her, her husband also. What does motherhood require? Transparent tenderness, authentic spirituality, inner confidence, unselfish love, self-control. Quite a list, isn't it? Almost more than we should expect. Perhaps that explains why Irma Bombeck used to say that motherhood takes 180 movable parts. and three pairs of hands and three sets of eyes. And I might add, the grace of God. If you happen to be a mother, here's one guy who applauds your every effort. Five cheers for all you do. Remember the skin horse and the velveteen rabbit? All his stuffing was starting to come out. His hair had been loved off, but how valuable he was. Carefully kept mothers don't have secure kids. Carefully kept untouched velveteen mothers turn out fragile. unselfish untouchable children but unselfish giving secure moms somehow managed to deposit healthy wholesome kids into our lonely frightened society so like uh diana said not to talk so much you know so that's why terry's been mr silent",
